      "id": 1,
      "text": "Williamson was founded as a coal town, its early economy built around mining the rich Southern Illinois coal seams.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamson%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name honors John and Matthew Williamson, the original landowners who settled the area in the early 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamson%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Williamson County’s history museum in Marion offers guided tours that showcase the region’s coal mining heritage and Native American artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.williamsoncountyil.gov/about-us/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The county seat, Marion, was established in 1839 and still hosts the historic courthouse that survived a 1875 fire that destroyed many records.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.williamsoncountyil.gov/about-us/history/",
